course: dictionary
lesson: 15046
title: Retractable: pulled back in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Long words often hide clues in their parts. Retractable comes from retract, which means pull back, and -able, which means can be. So retractable means able to be pulled back. «The pen has a retractable tip, so it is safe in your pocket.» The word pocket is a clue: the tip goes back in when you are not writing.
explain: «The cat kept its retractable claws tucked in while it slept.» Tucked in is another clue. Cats can pull their claws back in, so they are not sharp when the cat is resting.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try: «The pen has a tip that can be pulled back in, so it is safe in your pocket.» It still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: Retractable means able to be pulled back in or folded away when not in use.
fact: Retractable can also describe something that slides or rolls back into a case or body.
fact: Retractable comes from retract, meaning to pull back, and -able, meaning can be.
fact: Everyday examples include retractable pens, retractable dog leads, and stadium roofs that slide back.
fact: Cats have retractable claws, so they can pull them in when they are not needed.
exercise: «The retractable lead let the dog run ten metres and then rolled back in.» What does retractable mean? | Able to swim fast | Very heavy and hard to lift | *Able to be pulled back in | Painted bright red
exercise: «The stadium has a retractable roof that closes when it rains.» Which word shows the roof moves? | *closes | roof | stadium | rains
exercise: «Cats have retractable claws, so they can pull them in.» What does it mean for claws to be retractable? | They are long and sharp all the time | *They can be pulled back in | They are made of wood | They fall off every year
test: «The pen had a retractable tip, so it was safe in my bag.» What does retractable mean in this sentence? | Able to change colour | Able to be sharp for writing | Able to be lost easily | *Able to be pulled back in
test: Jamie says retractable is too hard. What is a good tip? | Ask someone to draw a picture of it only | Skip it and never think about it again | *Break it into parts: retract and -able | Guess that it means colourful
exam: Nina wrote, «The roof of the stadium is retractable.» What does this tell us? | It is very tall | *It can be pulled back or folded away | It is always open to the sky | It is made of glass
